<section id="Ax1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Infrastructure Details</h3>

<div id="Ax1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments were conducted on a dedicated high-performance computing environment:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Ax1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CPU:</span> Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6242 @ 2.80 GHz (x86_64)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPU:</span> NVIDIA Tesla V100 SXM2 with 32 GB VRAM</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CUDA:</span> Version 12.0</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>General Evaluation Benchmarks</h3>

<div id="Ax1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Detailed descriptions of the general evaluation benchmarks:</p>
</div>
<section id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">HellaSwag</h5>

<div id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zellers et al. (2019)</a></cite>
Evaluates commonsense natural language inference. Humans achieve <math id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math>95% accuracy, while the benchmark presents significant challenges for state-of-the-art language models in contextual reasoning and commonsense understanding.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LAMBADA</h5>

<div id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paperno et al. (2016)</a></cite>
Assesses broad discourse understanding through word prediction. Requires models to maintain coherence across extended contexts beyond immediate sentences. We use the <span id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lambada_openai</span> variant (OpenAI-processed test split).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MMLU</h5>

<div id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al. (2020)</a></cite>
Massive Multitask Language Understanding spanning 57 academic and professional disciplines. Evaluates both breadth and depth of knowledge across STEM, humanities, and social sciences, requiring strong reasoning and problem-solving capabilities.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Winogrande</h5>

<div id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sakaguchi et al. (2021)</a></cite>
Large-scale commonsense reasoning benchmark with 44,000 fill-in-the-blank problems. Addresses scale and bias issues from earlier Winograd Schema Challenge versions through careful dataset construction.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Ax1.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="Ax1.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
